Reliability, maintenance, and repair preserve or restore the useful performance of systems over time. The material connects failure modes, degradation, diagnostics, inspection, availability, and repair planning with technical documentation, skilled trades, workshops, spare-parts inventories, compatible replacements, fabrication, and logistics, showing how sustained capability depends on maintenance networks and feedback into design.

**Common preparation developed:** [Continuing-service investigation](../core/Investigate-operating-histories-repair-resources-and-service-evidence.lingua) joins first-failure/availability distinctions, censored exposure, conditional cycle-average and shared-support arguments, finite repair resources, diagnosis and return evidence. Four original mechanical service Records are reused with their specialist routes preserved. The common paper/software model is not measured reliability or physical commissioning. Full mechanisms, survival analysis, repair optimization, maintenance networks and advanced practical formation remain pending.

**Common preparation developed:** the [operating recovery lesson](../core/Recover-the-known-condition-rather-than-replaying-the-remembered-steps.lingua) distinguishes partly completed work, unresolved commands, physical observations and a defensible return condition. Its finite recovery-path proof assumes exact information and successful commands; real diagnosis, repair, isolation and return-to-service competence remain full branch work.

